{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-03T21:19:36.501Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"436e44ca2d204a1ee603915a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.317","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1655"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1655: SDK placeholder and type refusals name CLI flags, and parent: null is refused, so typed callers have no documented way to clear a field"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Since GH-1614 (pm-gh1614) typed PmClient fields keep CLI sentinels literal. Typed SDK callers now get refusals written for the CLI: create/update parent 'none' says 'Use --unset parent', an empty parent says 'Use --parent none to unset', a self-parent says 'Use --unset parent', a missing strict parent says 'use --parent none', and parent/assignee null fail a string type check (invalid_argument_value) instead of meaning 'no value'. assignee 'none' now stores a person called none with no advisory. Reproduced on 2026.11.3 dist in a sandbox tracker."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","gh:1655","refusals","sdk","sentinels"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-03T21:19:36.501Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-03T21:19:36.501Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":240},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Typed SDK create/update refusals for placeholder, empty and self parent name the SDK remedy (unset: ['parent'] or omit parent) and never a CLI flag, with a spec per refusal; A typed SDK null on a clearable scalar field (parent, assignee, and every field the unset list accepts) clears it exactly like unset: [field]; null on a field that cannot be cleared refuses naming the field, with specs; A typed SDK create/update whose clearable scalar equals a former clear sentinel (none, null, -) succeeds and returns a stable advisory warning naming the field and the unset form; CLI behaviour and wording are unchanged: --parent none still clears, and CLI refusals still name CLI flags, proven by the existing CLI specs; docs/SDK.md documents null-as-clear and the advisory, and the SDK surface snapshot records any type widening"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-9rgaal"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A typed SDK caller that hits a parent refusal is told the SDK form, and null clears a clearable field"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"create({parent:'none'}) refuses naming --unset parent; create({parent:null}) refuses 'create parent must be a string.'; create({assignee:'none'}) stores the literal silently"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1614","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-03T21:19:36.501Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"0b4cc5a1262be3b2005cb3abed31c5da94989be901719d82ee890ee3429adf71","item_hash_version":3,"message":"File GH-1655","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"0f21ff630bb9f2c7ea3c282db519053797c42dfb93eedfa8772e25f6cdcb9f96"}
